   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing by hand. The stereochemistry is only partly assigned: I assumed L-configuration for every amino acid and left the sugar stereocentres unspecified. I did not check any other wedge or hash against the drawing.\n\n**Peptide.** Reading from the N-terminus, the chain is His-Gln-Val-Cys-Leu-Ser-Tyr-Arg-Gly-Arg-Pro-Val-Cys-Phe-Ser-Thr-NH2. The two Cys residues are joined by a disulfide bond, and the C-terminus is a primary amide (Thr-NH2).\n\n**N-terminal linker.** The His N-terminus carries an acyl group, C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013cyclobutane\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2C(=O)NH\u2013. The cyclobutane is 1,3-disubstituted. One substituent is drawn hashed and the other wedged, so I wrote it as trans.\n\n**Branching core.** The amide nitrogen is attached to a quaternary carbon with three identical arms. Each arm is CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013C(=O)NH\u2013CH2CH2\u2013(OCH2CH2)3\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013 followed by a sugar.\n\n**Sugar.** Each sugar is a bicyclic anhydro-hexose. The ring carbons are the quaternary ketal carbon (bearing the CH2 that links to the PEG chain), the ring oxygen, the anomeric carbon, C2 (NHCOCF3), C3 (OH) and C4 (OH). A CH2\u2013O bridge links the ketal carbon to the anomeric carbon.\n\nSMILES: O=C(CCO[C@H]5C[C@@H](OCCC(=O)NC(COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOCC12COC(O1)C(NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)C(O)C2O)(COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOCC12COC(O1)C(NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)C(O)C2O)COCCC(=O)NCCOCCOCCOCCOCC12COC(O1)C(NC(=O)C(F)(F)F)C(O)C2O)C5)N[C@@H](Cc8c[nH]cn8)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS7)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc8ccc(O)cc8)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)NCC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCNC(N)=N)C(=O)N6CCC[C@H]6C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS7)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc8ccccc8)C(=O)N[C@@H](CO)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(N)=O"
